<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!-- Repair: point the standard "Quotation / Order" PDF back at Odoo's
         own template.

         This database carries a leftover write on sale.action_report_saleorder
         made by `aabaan_quotation_report`, a module of the *other* Odoo.sh
         project (core2plus-odoo-aabaan). It redirected the core action to its
         own letterhead template:

             report_name = aabaan_quotation_report.report_saleorder_aabaan

         An Odoo.sh project only loads its own addons path, so that module —
         and its template — do not exist here. The action, however, belongs to
         `sale`, not to that module, so nothing ever restored it: uninstalling
         or orphaning the module deletes the template and leaves the core
         action pointing at the hole. Every sale order in the database then
         fails to print with "Template not found:
         'aabaan_quotation_report.report_saleorder_aabaan'" — and because
         print, the Send-by-email attachment and the customer portal PDF all
         route through this one action, a customer could not be sent a
         quotation at all.

         Values restored verbatim from odoo/addons/sale/report/ir_actions_report.xml
         (19.0). paperformat_id is cleared rather than set: the core action
         declares none and falls back to the company default; the one it was
         given belongs to that other project too.

         Deliberately NOT noupdate: this re-applies on every upgrade, so if the
         database is ever re-seeded from an aabaan dump again it heals itself.

         If a branded quotation PDF is wanted on this build one day, it is a new
         report action of our own — not a second hijack of the core record.
         The FM Service Agreement and FM Quotation (fm_documents) are exactly
         that, and print from their own buttons on the FM contract. -->
    <record id="sale.action_report_saleorder" model="ir.actions.report">
        <field name="report_name">sale.report_saleorder</field>
        <field name="report_file">sale.report_saleorder</field>
        <field name="paperformat_id" eval="False"/>
    </record>

</odoo>
